  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAN BERNARDINO NEOTRPICAL MIG BIRD HABITAT RESTORATION IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will: 1) restore 500 acres of upland grasslands in Sonora, Mexico and 2,000 acres in Arizona that have not been part of previous NMBCA phases, 2) cultivate and harvest a native grass seed bank, 3) monitor grassland- and riparian-associated bird species on 15,000 acres, and 4) conduct outreach to local landowners and educational institutions to promote restoration of their lands. Sufficient cash match must be contributed for grant-funded activities in the USA to maintain a 3:1 ratio</narrative>
  </description>
